# pixel-keshet.co.il / pixel-led.co.il -> xvision.co.il
#
# The two rules that used to live here used absolute source URLs. Cloudflare rejects
# the ENTIRE _redirects file for that ("Only relative URLs are allowed", code 100324),
# which failed every deploy. They never worked on GitHub Pages either, since it ignores
# this file. A _redirects rule can only match paths on the site's own hostnames, so
# cross-domain forwarding cannot be expressed here at all.
#
# Handle it with a Cloudflare Redirect Rule instead (Rules -> Redirect Rules):
#   When:  http.host in {"pixel-keshet.co.il" "www.pixel-keshet.co.il"
#                        "pixel-led.co.il" "www.pixel-led.co.il"}
#   Then:  dynamic -> concat("https://xvision.co.il", http.request.uri.path)
#          status 301, preserve query string
# That also fixes the current behaviour, where those domains flatten every path to the
# homepage - which Google treats as a soft 404.

